  "cell": "contra_directional_coupler",
  "title": "Contra-directional coupler (add-drop filter)",
  "designers": "Mustafa Hammood (UBC), parametric cell; the device and its anti-reflection layout from Wei Shi et al. (UBC)",
  "refs": [
   "shi2013cdc",
   "shi2013cwdm"
  ],
  "blurb": "Two strips, 560 and 440 nm wide with a 100 nm gap, corrugated over 1000 periods of 316 nm (316 µm): the grating reflects one C-band channel from the forward mode of one guide into the backward mode of the other, an add-drop filter with no free spectral range. Each guide's two sidewalls are offset by half a period to cancel its own reflection, and a Gaussian apodisation leaves visible teeth (sidewall steps of up to 50 and 25 nm) only in the middle 80 µm or so.",
  "chapters": [
   [
    "Chapter 13 (Section 13.7)",
    "/part-3/ch13/#fig-13-7"
   ],
   [
    "Chapter 14",
    "/part-3/ch14/"
   ]
  ],
